You mean the effect on the shopkeeper's own wands, or the fact that
the player could hide behind the magic doorway as well?  I'm not
convinced the latter is that much of an issue, given that shops aren't
all that common in the dungeon.  As for the former, the obvious
solution is to dispense with the wands -- you just called them mostly
useless in your previous post.  Maybe give the shopkeepers crossbows
or something instead.

